  "id": "ttx",
  "term": "TTX",
  "definition": "TTX, or tetrodotoxin, is a neurotoxin that blocks fast voltage-gated sodium channels in nerve cell membranes, preventing nerve signals from being transmitted. It has potential pain-relieving activity and is produced by certain bacteria, although it is also found in animals such as pufferfish.",
